# Regression fixture for a null-pointer dereference found by fuzzing
# (fuzz/fuzz_pipeline.cpp, crash input derived from a mutated ex2.pudl).
# `&&` followed by `<=` fails to parse a right-hand side (`<=` can't
# start an expression) -- land()'s recursive call for the RHS returns
# NULL, which used to propagate up through cmp()/cmpeq()/additive()/
# multiplicative() as an unchecked lhs: every one of those dereferenced
# lhs->getType() without checking for NULL first.
func mast : int {
  bool b = True && <= 1
  return 0
}
